/-!
# Cohomology and completion of a coherent module on a Noetherian scheme over a Noetherian ring

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a Noetherian scheme over `A`
and `ℱ` a coherent `𝒪_X`-module all of whose cohomology modules `H^p(X, ℱ)` are finite over `A`.
Write `𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X` for the ideal sheaf generated by `I` and `ℱ / 𝓘ⁿℱ` for the quotients of `ℱ`
by its powers. Then for every `p` there is a short exact sequence of `A`-modules
`0 ⟶ R¹lim H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ H^p(X, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ lim H^p(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ 0`,
where `H^p(X, ℱ)^∧` is the `I`-adic completion of the `A`-module `H^p(X, ℱ)` and `R¹lim` is the
cokernel of `1 - shift` on the product of the tower.

Four ingredients enter. The ordinary inverse limit `lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ`, placed in degree zero, is the
derived limit of the tower ([Stacks, Tag 0A0K]); `A`-linear derived global sections carry that
derived limit to a derived limit in `D(A)` ([Stacks, Tag 08U1]); the cohomology of a derived
limit of a countable tower of complexes of modules sits in the Milnor short exact sequence
([Stacks, Tag 07KZ]); and the cohomology of the derived `I`-adic completion of a complex whose
cohomology modules are all finite is the `I`-adic completion of its cohomology ([Stacks,
Tag 0A06]). The last is the only place where finiteness of `H^p(X, ℱ)` over `A` is used.

The identification of `RΓ(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)` with the derived `I`-adic completion of `RΓ(X, ℱ)` is
[Stacks, Tag 0BLX]; it is not available in this library and is carried as the hypothesis `hBLX`
below. That hypothesis is an isomorphism between two objects of `D(A)`, and asserts nothing about
any exact sequence: the three terms of the conclusion and the exactness relating them come from
Tags 0A0K, 08U1, 07KZ and 0A06.

The vanishing of the `R¹lim` term for a proper `f` is not proved here. It rests on the
Mittag-Leffler condition for the tower `n ↦ H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)`, which is [Stacks, Tag 02OB]; for
a countable tower of modules the Mittag-Leffler condition is equivalent to the vanishing of
`R¹lim`, so the properness clause cannot be reduced to a hypothesis on the tower that is weaker
than its own conclusion.

## Main definitions

There are no new definitions. The tower of quotients is
`Stacks.Algebraization.adicQuotientSystem` for the ideal sheaf
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf`, the `R¹lim` term is
`CompletionSequences.firstDerivedLimit`, and derived global sections are
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedGlobalSectionsOver`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology`: the short exact sequence
  relating the `I`-adic completion of `H^p(X, ℱ)` to the inverse limit and the first derived
  inverse limit of the cohomology modules of the adic quotients.

## Implementation notes

Cohomology is taken as the cohomology of `A`-linear derived global sections, so all three terms
of the sequence are `A`-modules and the sequence is one of `A`-modules. The `R¹lim` term is the
cokernel model `CompletionSequences.firstDerivedLimit`, the cokernel of `1 - shift` on the
product of the tower; that is the model the Milnor sequence of [Stacks, Tag 07KZ] produces.

Derived `I`-adic completion is represented by an arbitrary left adjoint `C` to the inclusion of
the full subcategory of derived-complete objects, as in [Stacks, Tag 0A06], so neither the
statement nor the hypothesis `hBLX` depends on a choice of reflector.

Both derived categories are the standard model: `Stacks.Algebraization.modulesHasDerivedCategory`
is reinstated as a local instance of high priority so that `D(𝒪_X)` is the one at which
[Stacks, Tag 0A0K] is stated, rather than the locally small
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory` that instance search would otherwise
supply; `D(A)` is then the standard model too, which is the one [Stacks, Tag 0A06] uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A06](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A06)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08U1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08U1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local instance 10000] Stacks.Algebraization.modulesHasDerivedCategory

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-- A short exact sequence transports along an isomorphism of its middle term. -/
private lemma exists_shortExact_of_iso_middle
    {C : Type*} [Category C] [Abelian C] {L M M' R : C}
    (i : L ⟶ M) (q : M ⟶ R) (w : i ≫ q = 0)
    (hs : (ShortComplex.mk i q w).ShortExact) (e : M ≅ M') :
    ∃ (i' : L ⟶ M') (q' : M' ⟶ R) (w' : i' ≫ q' = 0),
      (ShortComplex.mk i' q' w').ShortExact := by
  refine ⟨i ≫ e.hom, e.inv ≫ q, by simp [w], ?_⟩
  exact ShortComplex.shortExact_of_iso
    (ShortComplex.isoMk (Iso.refl L) e (Iso.refl R) (by simp) (by simp)) hs

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0A0M**, the short exact sequence, granted [Stacks, Tag 0BLX].

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a Noetherian scheme over `A`
and `ℱ` a coherent `𝒪_X`-module whose cohomology modules `H^p(X, ℱ)` are finite over `A`. Write
`𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X`. Then for every `p` the `I`-adic completion of `H^p(X, ℱ)` sits in a short exact
sequence of `A`-modules
`0 ⟶ R¹lim H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ H^p(X, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ lim H^p(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ 0`
whose left term is the cokernel of `1 - shift` on the product of the degree-`(p-1)` cohomology
tower and whose right term is the inverse limit of the degree-`p` cohomology tower.

Derived `I`-adic completion is represented by an arbitrary left adjoint `C` to the inclusion of
the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`. The hypothesis `hBLX` is [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] for `f`: the
derived global sections of the formal completion `lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` are the derived `I`-adic completion
of the derived global sections of `ℱ`. -/
@[stacks 0A0M "the exact sequence, granted the identification of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] of the \
derived global sections of the formal completion with the derived I-adic completion of the \
derived global sections, carried as the hypothesis hBLX"]
public theorem exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsNoetherian X] (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A))
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    (hfinite : ∀ p : ℤ, Module.Finite A
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) p).obj
        ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F))))
    (C : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) ⥤
      (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
        fun L ↦ IsDerivedComplete I L).FullSubcategory)
    (adj : C ⊣ (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
      fun L ↦ IsDerivedComplete I L).ι)
    (hBLX : Nonempty
      ((C.obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F))).obj ≅
        (derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj
            (limit (adicQuotientSystem
              (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F)))))
    (p : ℤ) :
    let T : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
      adicQuotientSystem (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0 ⋙ derivedGlobalSectionsOver f
    let H : ℤ → DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A := fun q ↦
      DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) q
    ∃ (i : CompletionSequences.firstDerivedLimit A (T ⋙ H (p - 1)) ⟶
        ModuleCat.of A (AdicCompletion I
          ((H p).obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F)))))
      (q : ModuleCat.of A (AdicCompletion I
          ((H p).obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F)))) ⟶
        limit (T ⋙ H p))
      (w : i ≫ q = 0),
      (ShortComplex.mk i q w).ShortExact := by
  intro T H
  set single := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0
  set D := derivedGlobalSectionsOver f
  set S := adicQuotientSystem (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]: the ordinary limit of the adic quotient tower is its derived limit.
  obtain ⟨hprodSheaf, hlimSheaf⟩ :=
    isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients
      (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F
  -- [Stacks, Tag 08U1]: derived global sections carry that to a derived limit in `D(A)`.
  obtain ⟨hprod, hlim⟩ :=
    isDerivedLimit_map_derivedGlobalSectionsOver f (S ⋙ single) (single.obj (limit S)) hlimSheaf
  have hprod' : HasProduct fun n : ℕ ↦ T.obj ⟨n⟩ := hprod
  have hlim' : IsDerivedLimit T (D.obj (single.obj (limit S))) := hlim
  -- [Stacks, Tag 07KZ]: the Milnor short exact sequence of that derived limit.
  obtain ⟨-, hmilnor⟩ :=
    ModuleDerivedLimitTriangle.derivedLimit_iso_and_homology_shortExact.{u, u} A T
  obtain ⟨a, b, -, hdegree⟩ := hmilnor _ hlim'
  obtain ⟨-, i, q, w, -, -, -, hse⟩ := hdegree p
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] and [Stacks, Tag 0A06] identify the middle term.
  obtain ⟨eBLX⟩ := hBLX
  obtain ⟨eFin⟩ :=
    AdicCompletionCohomology.derivedCompletion_homology_iso_adicCompletion A I
      (D.obj (single.obj F)) hfinite C adj p
  exact exists_shortExact_of_iso_middle i q w hse (((H p).mapIso eBLX).symm ≪≫ eFin)

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
